//! task: write
//! ask: Return the first even number below n (or 0), using `perge` to skip odd numbers and `rumpe` to stop.
//! expect: ok
//! refs: §8.4, §8.5
//! explain: `perge` continues to the next iteration and `rumpe` leaves the loop; both are imperatives, as `redde` is (§8.5, "Mood"). `residuum` is integer remainder, one of the contextual words — it is an operator only in operator position. `rumpe` is forbidden inside an iteration carrying a `contrahe` (EXS-E0342); the spec says nothing against `perge`, and `exsc` accepts it there.

publica functio primum_par(n: u64) -> u64 {
    mutabilis r: u64 = 0;
    per i in 0..n {
        si i residuum 2 ne 0 {
            perge;
        }
        r = i;
        rumpe;
    }
    redde r;
}
